Reason:
The bug occurs because the code related to userfaultfd write protection (uffd-wp) markers is executed even when the `PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP` configuration is not enabled. This leads to warnings due to undefined behavior when the code attempts to handle page table entries (PTEs) that are not properly defined or supported in the current configuration.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
#ifdef CONFIG_PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP
    if (pte_swp_uffd_wp_any(pte) &&
        !(zap_flags & ZAP_FLAG_DROP_MARKER))
        set_huge_pte_at(mm, address, ptep,
                         make_pte_marker(PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP));
#endif
```
Reason:
The fix involves wrapping the code that handles the uffd-wp markers with a preprocessor directive (`#ifdef CONFIG_PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP`). This ensures that the code will only be compiled and executed if the `PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP` configuration is enabled, preventing the potential warnings and undefined behavior when this configuration is not present.


